#{[17592186430935 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430935 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430935 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e03f06d7-09f6-5991-8022-a31e044488bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430938 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430938 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430938 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ecbcc9d3-a1f4-5e44-b6a6-513ff6a3a28b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430939 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430939 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430939 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa91438f-d562-5478-84cb-9cc0479a64c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430941 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6f84ddbb-0ce0-5549-8bb9-1dfef0b987f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430946 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fc27d6bf-860e-505c-82f5-df4b985c7b2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430948 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430948 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162595" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430948 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430948 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=-1,$ $x=2,$ $y=0,$ $y=1,$ $z=-1,$ $z=2.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=y{z}^{2}\\,i-2yz\\,j+3{z}^{2}\\,k,$ find the flux of $F$ across $S.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430948 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09c354f4-ffe0-5d80-b23d-97b7671b8b06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430948 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =0+(-2z)+6z \\\\  & =4z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}4z\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}4z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{-1}^{2}4z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =(2-(-1))\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot [2{z}^{2}]_{z=-1}^{z=2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot (8-2) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430950 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430950 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430950 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430950 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=1,$ $y=1,$ $y=3,$ $z=0,$ $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(y+{z}^{2})\\,i-x\\,j+3{x}^{2}{e}^{z}\\,k,$ find the flux of $F$ across $S.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430950 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ce23f40-f256-54cd-9b13-888ae9d3dff9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430950 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{x}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =0+0+3{x}^{2}{e}^{z} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}3{x}^{2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}3{x}^{2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=0}^{x=1}\\cdot (3-1)\\cdot [{e}^{z}]_{z=0}^{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =({1}^{3}-{0}^{3})\\cdot 2\\cdot ({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot (3-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537214 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186538010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537214 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186538017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759